  "verbalization": "Vibsanin Q is shown to interact with Hepatocyte, which is the target of two distinct compounds: 2-Nonyl-4-hydroxyquinoline N-oxide and (2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[...]-methoxy]-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol. Both of these compounds are identified as targets of Carboxylesterase 2, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving Carboxylesterase 2. The evidence indicates that Vibsanin Q may exert its effects through a pathway that leads to the inhibition of Carboxylesterase 2, possibly by modulating the activity of Hepatocyte, which is the common target of multiple compounds that interact with Carboxylesterase 2. The presence of multiple pathways converging on Carboxylesterase 2, along with the shared target of Hepatocyte, supports the hypothesis that Vibsanin Q may act by targeting Hepatocyte and thereby influencing Carboxylesterase 2 activity. The mechanism is supported by the observed final scores, which suggest a plausible and consistent relationship between Vibsanin Q and Carboxylesterase 2.",
